    "The Three-Body Problem": {
        curatorTitle: "Science on a Cosmic Scale",
        curatorNote: "The opening chapter of the hardest sci-fi series in recent memory. It starts slow with the Cultural Revolution but builds into a mind-bending exploration of physics, first contact, and existential dread. It's worth noting that President Obama has made several comments on The Three-Body Problem over time, leading to speculation that the books might be more than pure science fiction!<br><br><strong>Remembrance of Earth's Past Series:</strong><br>• <a href='/book/the-three-body-problem-cixin-liu/'>The Three-Body Problem</a> (Book 1)<br>• <a href='/book/the-dark-forest-cixin-liu/'>The Dark Forest</a> (Book 2)<br>• <a href='/book/deaths-end-cixin-liu/'>Death's End</a> (Book 3)<br>• <a href='/book/the-redemption-of-time-baoshu/'>The Redemption of Time</a> (Book 4)",
        narrator: "Daniel York Loh, P.J. Ochlan, Bruno Roubicek",
        soundCheck: "A Note on the Audio Editions: Please verify which narrator is listed on your store page before purchasing, as the \"official\" voice of the series varies significantly by region. US listeners will typically encounter P.J. Ochlan, who also narrated books 2 and 3 of the main trilogy, offering a consistent listening experience. UK/International listeners face a starker transition: while the main trilogy was recently re-recorded by Daniel York Loh to modernise the series, this finale retains the original performance by Bruno Roubicek. If you have just finished the high-energy Daniel York Loh versions, be prepared for a shift to Roubicek’s slower, more classical \"BBC-style\" delivery."
    },
